  "content": "The duo effectively turned the journalist into a crash-test dummy by demonstrating how they could remotely hack a 2014 Jeep Cherokee he was driving on the freeway, bringing the car to a full stop. They also gained control of the steering, high beams, turn signals, windshield wipers and fluid, door locks, and the speedometer and tachometer; and they showed how they could kill the engine and disengage the transmission so the accelerator pedal failed — and they did it all from Miller’s living room in St. Louis.",
